.TH KTEST 1
.SH NAME
ktest \- checks of the kernel's thread services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktest
.I check
.RI [ threads ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ktest
checks what programs rely on from the kernel, and prints
.B "ktest NAME: ok"
or
.BR "... FAIL" .
.I threads
is 1 to 64 (default 16). The checks:
.TP
.B fpu
Many threads compute in floating point at once, preempted; each result
must equal the same computation done again alone, bit for bit.
.TP
.B avx
The 16 AVX registers hold a pattern through a long busy loop (x86-64,
not in the build by sicc).
.TP
.B tls
Thread-local variables: each thread its own copy.
.TP
.B quota
A child limited to 16 MiB gets about that much, and cannot give its own
child more.
.TP
.B ipc
The message round trip between two threads, with and without floating
point and AVX.
.TP
.BR ipcmany " [" \fIn\fR ]
.I n
client threads (default 40) calling one server thread at once: the time
per call.
.TP
.B place
P-cores and E-cores (boot with
.BI pcores= n
where all cores are alike).
.TP
.B log
The console's log
.RB ( SYS_LOG ).
.TP
.B sig
Signals: caught, ignored, default, the waits they interrupt, a process
group, registers through a storm of them.
.TP
.B vm
Anonymous memory given on first touch,
.BR MAP_FIXED ,
faults that still end a process.
.TP
.B futex
A futex mutex shared by 8 threads, time limits, a thread's end waking
its joiner.
.TP
.B shm
Shared memory between two processes, notes, the wall clock, code shared
between two processes started from one image.
.TP
.BR hang " " spin | sleep | read | net
Wait forever (for Ctrl-C).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the check passed; 1 if not; 2 for an unknown check.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro (2)
